### 3★ Guesthouses and Smaller Hotels

Prices range from approximately CZK 1,200 to 2,000 (€50–80) per night. Accommodation tends to be comfortable, with clean and well-equipped rooms. Guests book treatments separately at the municipal spa or at partner facilities. Meals are usually provided as breakfast or half board.

### 4★ Hotels (Ensana Centrální Lázně, Ensana Hvězda, Ensana Butterfly)

Approximate prices from CZK 2,000 to 3,200 (€80–130) per night. These hotels usually have their own spa department, swimming pool, and wellness centre. Packages include half or full board, a medical consultation, and a set number of treatments per day. The Ensana Centrální Lázně hotel is directly connected to the historic treatment centre.

### 5★ Hotel Ensana Nové Lázně

The flagship of the spa complex, with prices from approximately CZK 3,200 to 5,000 (€130–200) per night. Guests have access to the unique Roman Thermal Bath, the Royal Cabin, and the complete spectrum of medical treatments. Fine-dining cuisine, a personalised therapy programme, and premium services round out the experience.

### Treatments Booked Separately

If you are staying in a guesthouse or smaller hotel without its own spa department, you can buy treatments on top. Approximate prices for treatment packages range from CZK 5,000 to 12,500 (€200–500) per week, depending on the number and type of procedures.

## What Is Typically Included

Spa packages in Mariánské Lázně usually include:

- **Accommodation** in a room of the chosen category
- **Meals** — half board (breakfast and dinner) or full board
- **Initial medical consultation** — examination and preparation of a treatment plan
- **Spa treatments** — typically 2–3 procedures per day (depending on the stay length and package)
- **Pool and wellness access** — indoor pool, sauna, steam bath, fitness centre
- **Drinking cure** — access to the [mineral springs](/en/mineral-springs) is free of charge for all visitors

Some packages additionally include a final medical check-up, recommendations for home care, and transfers from the railway station.

### Typical Surcharges

- Premium treatments (specialist massages, cosmetic procedures)
- Single room (supplement of approximately CZK 300–800 per night)
- Room with a view of the Colonnade or the park
- Special diets beyond the standard menu

## Seasonal Prices — When to Visit and Save

Prices in Mariánské Lázně vary considerably by season. By choosing your dates wisely you can save up to 30% of the total cost of your stay.

### Peak Season (June–September, Christmas and New Year)

The highest prices and strongest demand. The town is at its most beautiful — the Colonnade comes alive with musical performances, the parks are in bloom, and the Singing Fountain plays every odd-numbered day. We recommend booking at least 2–3 months in advance.

### Shoulder Season (April–May, October)

An excellent compromise between price and weather. Prices are approximately 10–15% lower than in peak season. Spring brings blooming magnolias in Skalník Park, while autumn enchants with the colours of the surrounding forests. Fewer tourists mean calmer treatment sessions and more attention from staff.

### Low Season (November–March, Excluding Holidays)

The best prices — savings of 20–30% compared with peak season. The town has its own special charm in winter as well: snow-covered colonnades, Christmas markets, and warm mineral baths that contrast with the crisp air. The ideal time for those seeking peace and maximum value for money.

