## Health Insurance Contribution

Important information for Czech citizens: **health insurance companies contribute to spa treatment** when it is prescribed by an attending physician. There are two main types:

- **Comprehensive Spa Treatment (KLP)** — the insurance company covers treatment, accommodation, and meals. The patient pays only a regulatory fee (approximately CZK 100/day). Requires an indication from a specialist and approval by a review doctor.
- **Contributory Spa Treatment (PLP)** — the insurance company covers the medical procedures, while the patient pays for accommodation and meals. A more accessible option that only requires a recommendation from a general practitioner.

In addition, most insurance companies offer contributions towards preventive and wellness stays as part of their bonus programmes — typically CZK 2,000 to 5,000 per year. Check with your insurance provider for current conditions.

## Tips for Saving Money

### Book in Advance

Booking 2–3 months ahead unlocks early-bird discounts that can reach 10–15% of the total cost. Some hotels offer preferential rates for bookings made as much as 6 months in advance.

### Consider a Longer Stay

The longer your stay, the lower the price per night. With three-week cures, the nightly rate is usually 15–25% lower than for weekend stays. As a bonus, the therapeutic effects come fully into play.

### Take Advantage of the Low Season

As mentioned above, stays outside the peak season are 20–30% cheaper. The healing effects of the mineral springs do not depend on the time of year — they work the same all year round.

### Loyalty Programmes

Returning guests often receive preferential conditions. Ask about loyalty discounts, special offers for repeat stays, and referral programmes.

### Watch for Current Offers

Spa hotels regularly publish seasonal promotions and last-minute deals. It pays to follow the websites of individual hotels and subscribe to newsletters.

## What Affects the Total Cost

When planning your budget, don't forget to factor in other expenses:

- **Travel** — the train journey from Prague takes approximately 3 hours, with tickets from CZK 350. The bus is even cheaper. By car, allow for motorway tolls and parking (approximately CZK 150–300/day).
- **Spending money** — for coffee on the Colonnade, souvenirs, spa wafers, and any trips into the surrounding area, allow approximately CZK 500–1,000 per day.
- **Premium treatments** — if you would like procedures beyond your package, allow approximately CZK 500–2,000 per treatment.
- **Spa tax** — approximately CZK 15 per person per night (paid on site).

## Who a Spa Stay Is Worth It For

A spa stay in Mariánské Lázně is not a needless luxury — it is an investment in your health with measurable results. The mineral springs, CO₂ baths, and expert medical care help with musculoskeletal complaints, kidney and urinary tract conditions, respiratory problems, and lifestyle-related illnesses.

Compared with the cost of long-term medication or regular physiotherapy visits, a three-week cure is often an economically advantageous alternative — with the added value of resting in a beautiful setting.

## Practical Planning Information

When planning a spa stay we recommend:

1. **Consult your doctor** — ideally 2–3 months before your planned departure, especially if you would like to use your insurance contribution
1. **Compare offers** from several hotels and spa houses
1. **Check the cancellation conditions** — most hotels allow free cancellation up to 14–30 days before arrival
1. **Read more** about [accommodation](/en/accommodation) and [practical advice](/en/practical-info) for visitors

Mariánské Lázně combines more than two centuries of spa tradition with modern facilities and a level of affordability that is exceptional in the Central European context. Whether you are looking for a short wellness escape or a comprehensive treatment programme, you will find an option that matches both your needs and your budget.

For up-to-date information on prices and spa programmes, visit the [official website of the Léčebné lázně](https://www.lazneml.cz).

> **The prices given in this article are approximate and based on data valid at the start of 2026. Actual prices may vary by season, room type, chosen package, and the current offers of individual hotels.**
